      "created_at": "2020-06-02T09:27:34Z",
      "updated_at": "2020-06-02T09:27:34Z",
      "body": "I don't think that this will be enough. Even though you can get the consent and update the status accordingly, there is currently no way of forwarding the status of consent to this library, so that the actual ad request receives the status. \r\n\r\nCould you implement a simple personalized/non-personalized prop to the NativeAdView component? I think this can easily be achieved by simply adding a URL parameter to the request.\r\n\r\nFrom the React Native Firebase SDK: \r\n\r\n> The requested ad URL via the SDK will send a request with an additional parameter &npa=1, which will return a non-personalized ad.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
